# Template for .env.local — personal settings and secrets, git-ignored.
#   make setup   (copies this file to .env.local if it does not exist yet)
# Committed local defaults (ports, localhost DB/Redis, TTLs) live in .env and need no copy.
# Precedence: shell environment > .env.local > .env. Canon of keys: internal/config/config.go.
# Render stage: every value comes from the Dashboard (render.yaml `sync: false`); files are not used.

# Required. HS256 key, at least 32 bytes. Also signs avatar and client-analytics links.
# Render stage: sync:false (openssl rand -hex 32)
JWT_SECRET=

# Optional overrides of the committed defaults in .env — uncomment what you need.
# TRAINER_INVITE_TTL_DAYS=1
# CORS_ALLOW_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173

# Telegram bot. All empty = bot disabled locally (push and webhook off).
# Render stage: sync:false (stage bot, без @)
TELEGRAM_BOT_USERNAME=
# Render stage: sync:false (@BotFather)
BOT_TOKEN=
# Render stage: https://mentorix-api-stage.onrender.com/telegram/webhook
BOT_WEBHOOK_URL=
# Render stage: sync:false (openssl rand -hex 32)
BOT_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Frontend page for client self-analytics (Telegram «Статистика» button). Empty = button hidden.
# Absolute http(s) URL without query/fragment, e.g. http://localhost:5173/stats
# Render stage: sync:false — stage frontend origin + page path; that origin must also be in CORS_ALLOW_ORIGINS
CLIENT_ANALYTICS_PAGE_URL=
